# Cloudflare Pages. Every public page is a file of its own in the build
# (about.html answers /about, and so on: scripts/prerender.mjs), so the pages
# need no line here. Anything that is neither a file nor listed below gets
# 404.html and a 404 status, so the app's "Page not found" screen is not
# reported to browsers and search engines as a working page.
#
# The one address with no file is an old listing link. The app has no listing
# pages of its own (listings open inside the Georgia MLS search), so the link
# is sent on to the search page. 302, not 301: browsers keep a 301 for good,
# and a listing page may exist one day.
# A new <Route> in src/App.js needs a page in src/lib/pageMeta.js or a line
# here; src/PublicRoutes.test.js fails until it has one.
/property/* /search 302
